  "steps": [
   "Heat the oven to 190°C (170°C fan). Halve the grapes and tip them into a medium baking dish with the blackberries.",
   "Squeeze over the lemon juice, sprinkle on the cornflour and half the cinnamon, and toss until the fruit is lightly coated.",
   "In a bowl, mix the oats, flour, almonds, sugar, the rest of the cinnamon and the salt. Pour in the oil and rub it through with your fingertips until the mix clumps into rough crumbs.",
   "Scatter the crumble evenly over the fruit without pressing it down.",
   "Bake for 25 to 30 minutes, until the topping is golden and crisp and purple juice bubbles up at the edges. Leave to cool for 10 minutes before spooning into bowls. It is just as good cold the next day."
